                <pb facs="0500" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 351.117/27.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Sharp</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>452. Mr. Herrick’s despatch 767, November 17. Ask release Chandeysson, now in
                    120th French Territorials, and permission immediate return this country.
                    Department informed important interests here need his attention. See
                    Department’s telegram December 31 concerning August Peralme.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
